# ── .NET ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
bin/
obj/
*.user
*.suo
.vs/
*.DotSettings.user
.sonarqube/
# Coverage output. `tests/**` alone let an SDK run's copy reach a commit — the sdk/ projects
# write here too, and the Sonar scan reads it from wherever it lands.
**/TestResults/
.idea/

# ── Node / Frontend ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/
dist/

# Generated by `npm run test:coverage`, and read by the Sonar scan from there. Regenerated on
# every run, so there is nothing to keep.
coverage/
.vite/
*.local

# ── Helm charts (downloaded at deploy time) ───────────────────────────────────
deploy/rediensiam/charts/

# ── Secrets / env ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.env
.env.*
*.pfx
*.key
deploy/rediensiam/values.secret.yaml
deploy/rediensiam/values.prod.secret.yaml
# Operator decisions written by deploy/setup.sh — hostnames, issuer names, backup
# destination. Not secrets, but per-installation: committing one makes the next
# operator inherit somebody else's hostname.
deploy/rediensiam/values.dev.override.yaml
deploy/rediensiam/values.prod.override.yaml
.sonar.env

# ── OS ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

deploy/rediensiam/tmpcharts-*/

# Rust SDK build artifacts
sdk/rust/**/target/
sdk/typescript/**/dist/
sdk/typescript/**/node_modules/
# Audit reports are kept in-tree as evidence; superseded sessions are not.
.security-hardening-archive-*/

# Editor/backup copies — one `cp values.secret.yaml values.secret.yaml.bak` from being a leak
*.bak

# April 2026 planning scratch from a UI overhaul; superseded and confusing next to
# .security-hardening/. Ignored so they do not come back.
findings.md
progress.md
task_plan.md

# A directory literally named `bin\Debug` — a Windows path that reached a Linux
# filesystem as one name. It is not matched by `**/bin`, so Docker copies it into
# the image, MSBuild cannot enumerate it, and every default glob reaches csc as a
# literal: `CS2021: File name '**/*.cs' is empty…`. It broke the image build once
# before (e170fcf) and came back through a `git add -A`.
*\\*
